Halving the penalty gives 17 change points, several about two weeks apart, which is the signature of the model chasing noise. The minimum length matters too, with 9, 5 and 3 change points at lengths 5, 10 and 20. Five change points in 500 returns is also close to the average the simulation below produces on fat-tailed data with no regime change at all, so the count by itself proves nothing. The scan separates the features that survive from the ones that do not: the early-2026 volatility swing is supported across most settings, the autumn 2025 calming is approximate, and the April 2025 spike is borderline.
